    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104253" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόμ-ιον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>victim cut up</i> for sacrifice,
			over which oaths were taken, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόμιον
				ἐντέμνεσθαι</span> to cut <i>such a victim</i> in pieces,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				192
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τ.</span> the <i>parts of the
				victim</i> used at this solemnity, ib.<i><span class="en">
				186
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.88
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				753d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				55.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στὰς ἐπὶ τῶν τ. κάπρου καὶ κριοῦ καὶ
					ταύρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					23.68
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				5.24.9
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>small log</i> or <i>block of wood,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				11(2).199
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				219
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				14
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>).</div>
